      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "In rural area, you need to know if your transformer will accept power input back to the grid, it may trip out your solar system.Second issue is; are the power lines to the house large enough to be able to take the power back to the grid, without blowing your house systems.These are very important issues that Central West Solar  management raised when completing an on site inspection.  No other company was aware of these problems.In other words, it appears that local knowledge may be better.At the moment I am making inquiries about up grading my power lines, they are very old and not large enough to handle the 10kw system.  Once I have upgraded my lines and installed my system I may be able to give a better response.",
